{
  "plancraftGrid": 1,
  "name": "Retirement decision grid v3",
  "description": "Corrected FERS (7/8 VA appointment, service from 2023, high-3 = FTE base+market $275k per 38 USC 7431(f); deferred annuities payable at 60 with 20+ yrs / 62 with 10-19 yrs, deflated 2.4%/yr from separation) plus Social Security claimed at 70 for both spouses. Simone's benefit reflects her later US career start (~2022): $4,100/mo real if she works to 60, $2,700/mo if she stops in 2038; her own benefit beats the spousal top-up in both patterns. Michael's SS varies with retirement age ($3,900-$5,100/mo). Disability: income stops 2033; DI nets $25k/yr savings then $180k/yr to 65; FERS $1,278/mo from 62; SS $2,900/mo from 70. New in v3: college top-up dimension - out-of-pocket college costs beyond the 529 ($1,300/mo/child birth-18 assumed to cover a baseline), at $0 / $25k / $50k per year per child in real dollars over each child's college years (child 1: Sep 2045 - Jun 2049; child 2: Sep 2047 - Jun 2051), modeled as essential expenses so they hit legacy and lifestyle spending, not the spending metric itself. Base otherwise unchanged: house June 2027, 2 kids, savings +2.5%/yr real, PA. SS amounts are scheduled-benefit estimates; trust-fund shortfall (~20% cut in the 2030s absent reform) is not modeled.",
